  "_comment": [
    "Order & Conquest — authored 42-territory board.",
    "ASSERTED TOTALS: 42 territories, 6 continents, 83 land-adjacency edges.",
    "Continent sizes NA 9 / SA 4 / EU 7 / AF 6 / AS 12 / AU 4.",
    "Continent bonuses 5 / 2 / 5 / 3 / 7 / 2. Border counts 3 / 2 / 4 / 3 / 5 / 1.",
    "",
    "'neighbours' is the LAND ADJACENCY GRAPH. It is the graph used by normal attack,",
    "by fortification, and by Air Force range. It is symmetric and validated on load.",
    "",
    "'crossesWater' is a RENDER HINT ONLY (draw the edge dashed). It is a subset of",
    "'neighbours' and has no mechanical meaning whatsoever. It is NOT a sea route.",
    "",
    "SEA ROUTES are a separate edge type. They do not appear in this file. They are",
    "generated per match from the seat-chosen count and frozen into matches.effective_map.",
    "See docs/07-game-design.md section 7.10.",
    "",
    "'capabilities' is the territory's capability profile. It is authored explicitly here",
    "and ALSO re-derived on load by rule CAP-1 and asserted equal (test TC-MAP-05):",
    "    profile = {Infantry} union ({NavalForce} if coastal) union {cardSymbol}",
    "Infantry / Cavalry / Artillery are card symbols only and grant no action (classic RISK).",
    "AirForce and NavalForce are the two capabilities that unlock actions.",
    "",
    "'shape' (SVG path) is deliberately absent. Adjacency ships first, artwork in Phase 12.",
    "'label' is an approximate anchor for the debug board view and for the army-count badge."
  ],

